(Regression test: Print on a buffer that had been cleared and rewritten
with fewer bytes was leaking stale data through the old NUL-scanning
path. Three separate code paths each had this bug - all three are
covered here.)

Create a buffer called buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 3 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 4 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 5 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 6 of buf to 'f'.

(Path 1: direct Print of a buffer variable)
Print buf.
clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'a'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'b'.
Print buf.

(Re-fill for format string tests)
clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 3 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 4 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 5 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 6 of buf to 'f'.

(Path 2: format-string variable interpolation)
Print "fmt-var: {buf}".
clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'c'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'd'.
Print "fmt-var: {buf}".

(Re-fill for expression path test)
clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 3 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 4 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 5 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 6 of buf to 'f'.

(Path 3: format-string expression)
a number called n is 1.
Print "fmt-expr: {buf}".
clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'e'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'f'.
Print "fmt-expr: {buf}".
